# limits.defaults - defaults of the settings of the loop IOC, in autosave's file format.
#
# Restored at every IOC start, before the file that autosave writes at run time
# ($MIST2_SAVE/iocLoop/limits.sav), whose values win. One line per PV: <PV name> <value>, in the
# unit of the PV. Where each value comes from: docs/emulation/LOOP.md, "Settings".
#
# ASSUMED: the gains come from the plant MODEL of the emulation (emulation/sim/config/plant.yaml,
# python3 emulation/sim/tools/plant_step_response.py), not from MIST-2. Measure the step response
# on the machine and set them again (LOOP.md, "Tuning on the machine").
#
# Discharge loop: set point 18 A. Its maximum is 22 A, below the 24 A full scale of the REK150-24:
# at 24 A the REK goes into constant current, more filament current cannot raise the discharge
# current, and a loop there can only act downward (docs/emulation/STATUS.md).
LOOP-DIS:value:setpoint 18
LOOP-DIS:value:setpoint.DRVL 0
LOOP-DIS:value:setpoint.DRVH 22
# SIMC rules for the model at its steepest point (gain 3.56 A/A, time constant 1.45 s, dead time
# about 0.3 s with the polling and the period) and a closed-loop time constant of 0.5 s.
LOOP-DIS:kp:setpoint 0.5
LOOP-DIS:ki:setpoint 0.35
# A first-order plant needs no derivative: off. The filter time (free choice, one period) is
# used once Kd is set.
LOOP-DIS:kd:setpoint 0
LOOP-DIS:dfilter:setpoint 0.2
# Output: at most 90 A, the filament current of the owner's working point (2026-11-21); at least
# 80 A (free choice: below the model's 12 A point at 85.8 A, the filament stays hot).
LOOP-DIS:outmin:setpoint 80
LOOP-DIS:outmax:setpoint 90
# 1 A/s of filament current (free choice: about 3 A/s of discharge current in the model).
LOOP-DIS:slew:setpoint 1
# Three missed counts of the platform IOC's heartbeat (once per second): hand back (free choice).
LOOP-DIS:stale:setpoint 3
<END>
